---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import '../styles/global.css';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const aircraftExterior = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8b/Piper_PA-28_Cherokee_-_G-BCPG_-_2_October_2025.jpg';
const aircraftCockpit = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/29/Cockpit_of_Piper_PA-28-151_%28G-BOYH%29_at_Bristol_Airport%2C_England_15May2016_arp.jpg';
const aircraftLanding = 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/24/Piper_PA-28_Cherokee_Landing_03.JPG';
---
<BaseLayout title="About Tyler | Hutzell Aviation" description="Learn about Tyler Hutzell, his ATP training background, and the purpose behind Hutzell Aviation aircraft rental in Athens, Georgia.">
  <Header />
  <main>
    <PageHero eyebrow="ABOUT HUTZELL AVIATION" title="Built by a pilot, for pilots who need access." description="Tyler Hutzell founded Hutzell Aviation to create a simpler, more professional path to renting an aircraft and building flight time in the Athens area." />

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container biography-grid">
        <div class="bio-visual reveal">
          <figure class="portrait-photo"><img src={`${base}images/tyler-hutzell.png`} alt="Tyler Hutzell, founder of Hutzell Aviation" width="400" height="400" decoding="async" /><figcaption><span>Tyler Hutzell</span><small>Founder, Hutzell Aviation LLC</small></figcaption></figure>
          <div class="bio-credential"><Icon name="plane" size={25} /><div><strong>ATP-trained pilot</strong><span>Exact training details to be added</span></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="bio-copy reveal reveal-delay">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> MEET THE OWNER</p>
          <h2>{site.owner}</h2>
          <p class="lead">Tyler completed professional flight training through ATP Flight School and understands how important consistent aircraft access can be for pilots working toward career and experience goals.</p>
          <p>Hutzell Aviation is being developed as an aircraft-rental company—not a flight school. The company’s purpose is to make the rental process clear, give qualified pilots a professional way to review availability, and offer flexible pricing for pilots who plan to fly regularly.</p>
          <p>The final biography can include Tyler’s ATP location, graduation date, certificates, ratings, total time, and the story of how he acquired the Piper Cherokee.</p>
          <div class="bio-values"><div><Icon name="shield" size={22} /><span><strong>Responsible access</strong>Approval and policies before booking.</span></div><div><Icon name="calendar" size={22} /><span><strong>Clear scheduling</strong>Availability that renters can understand.</span></div><div><Icon name="gauge" size={22} /><span><strong>Time-builder focused</strong>Packages designed around consistent flying.</span></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section purpose-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading centered reveal"><p class="eyebrow centered-eyebrow light"><span></span> THE COMPANY PURPOSE <span></span></p><h2>Aircraft access without presenting as a flight school.</h2><p>Every section of the site is written around aircraft rental, approved-renter access, and pilot time building.</p></div>
        <div class="purpose-grid"><article class="reveal"><span>01</span><h3>Dependable access</h3><p>Build a professional reservation process around one well-presented aircraft.</p></article><article class="reveal reveal-1"><span>02</span><h3>Transparent expectations</h3><p>Publish qualifications, policies, pricing terms, and aircraft information clearly.</p></article><article class="reveal reveal-2"><span>03</span><h3>Flexible time building</h3><p>Support both occasional renters and pilots purchasing larger hour blocks.</p></article></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section gallery-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading reveal"><p class="eyebrow"><span></span> PHOTO GALLERY</p><h2>A first look at Tyler and the aircraft platform.</h2><p>Tyler’s portrait is current. The Piper Cherokee images are representative filler photography and should be replaced with photos of the actual rental aircraft before the final launch.</p></div>
        <div class="gallery-grid">
          <figure class="gallery-photo wide"><img src={aircraftExterior} alt="Representative Piper PA-28 Cherokee parked on an airfield" width="4259" height="2842" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Representative Piper Cherokee exterior</figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="gallery-photo"><img src={aircraftCockpit} alt="Representative Piper PA-28 cockpit and instrument panel" width="3852" height="2564" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Representative PA-28 panel</figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="gallery-photo portrait-tile"><img src={`${base}images/tyler-hutzell.png`} alt="Tyler Hutzell" width="400" height="400" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Tyler Hutzell</figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="gallery-photo"><img src={aircraftLanding} alt="Representative Piper PA-28 Cherokee landing" width="1600" height="1200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Representative aircraft in operation</figcaption></figure>
          <figure class="gallery-photo aircraft-detail-crop"><img src={aircraftExterior} alt="Close crop of a representative Piper PA-28 Cherokee" width="4259" height="2842" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Exterior detail</figcaption></figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <CallToAction title="Interested in becoming a renter?" text="Review the aircraft and availability, then send Tyler the information needed to begin the approval process." />
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
